<title>USA: MGE wheat/barley/shrimp deliveries - Sept 25.</title>
<headline>MGE wheat/barley/shrimp deliveries - Sept 25.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Minneapolis Grain Exchange Grain reported the following deliveries against September futures (wheat in 000 bu, shrimp in lots) -</p>
<p>SPRING WHEAT - Oldest long - Sept 4, 1996.</p>
<p>WHITE WHEAT - Benson Quinn/h delivered 400,000 bu to Country Hedging/h. Oldest long - Aug 29, 1996.</p>
<p>BLACK TIGER SHRIMP - Cargill/c delivered 4 lots to Cargill/c. Oldest long - August 13, 1996.</p>
<p>BARLEY - Oldest long - August 2, 1996.</p>
<p>WHITE SHRIMP - Nil.</p>
<p>H=House. C=Customer account.</p>
<p>(Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720)</p>
</text>
